ogies, Inc. is a U.S.-based company that specializes in the design, engineering, and production of innovative electric aircraft platforms and integrated propulsion systems for the aviation sector. Its comprehensive product portfolio encompasses various electric aerial vehicles, advanced electric propulsion units, charging infrastructure, and essential components. The company's electric aircraft offerings include the piloted ALIA-CTOL (CX300), which is designed for freight operations, and the adaptable ALIA VTOL (A250), a vertical takeoff and landing model suitable for cargo, logistics, medical missions, and passenger services. For military applications, BETA provides the ALIA Defense VTOL (MV250), tailored for defense logistics and larger aircraft support. Beyond complete aircraft, BETA produces specialized components such as the H500A and V600 motors, which find application in both aerospace and marine environments, alongside proprietary battery systems for its electric aircraft. Its charging solutions include the \"charge cube,\" \"thermal management system cube,\" and \"mini cubes.\" The company also supplies ground support equipment and sophisticated flight control systems. BETA Technologies engages with a diverse clientele, selling its aircraft to military and commercial entities. It provides replacement battery units to operators, supplies propulsion systems to other electric vertical takeoff and landing (eVTOL) manufacturers, and distributes charging equipment to state authorities, operators, Fixed Base Operators (FBOs), and other electric aviation companies. The company's operations span four key aerospace sectors: cargo and logistics, medical services, defense, and passenger transport. Furthermore, BETA offers thorough training programs utilizing flight simulators and virtual reality technologies. Established in 2017, BETA Technologies is based in South Burlington, Vermont.","description_en":"BETA Technologies, Inc. is a U.S.-based company that specializes in the design, engineering, and production of innovative electric aircraft platforms and integrated propulsion systems for the aviation sector. Its comprehensive product portfolio encompasses various electric aerial vehicles, advanced electric propulsion units, charging infrastructure, and essential components. The company's electric aircraft offerings include the piloted ALIA-CTOL (CX300), which is designed for freight operations, and the adaptable ALIA VTOL (A250), a vertical takeoff and landing model suitable for cargo, logistics, medical missions, and passenger services. For military applications, BETA provides the ALIA Defense VTOL (MV250), tailored for defense logistics and larger aircraft support. Beyond complete aircraft, BETA produces specialized components such as the H500A and V600 motors, which find application in both aerospace and marine environments, alongside proprietary battery systems for its electric aircraft. Its charging solutions include the \"charge cube,\" \"thermal management system cube,\" and \"mini cubes.\" The company also supplies ground support equipment and sophisticated flight control systems. BETA Technologies engages with a diverse clientele, selling its aircraft to military and commercial entities. It provides replacement battery units to operators, supplies propulsion systems to other electric vertical takeoff and landing (eVTOL) manufacturers, and distributes charging equipment to state authorities, operators, Fixed Base Operators (FBOs), and other electric aviation companies. The company's operations span four key aerospace sectors: cargo and logistics, medical services, defense, and passenger transport. Furthermore, BETA offers thorough training programs utilizing flight simulators and virtual reality technologies. Established in 2017, BETA Technologies is based in South Burlington, Vermont.","description_zh":"BETA Technologies, Inc.（美股代碼：BETA）為 Industrials 領域之重要企業，專注於 Aerospace & Defense 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"1150